-- Common command invariant (all owner-authorized mutations):
-- command.verification_state = 'VERIFIED'
-- command.command_type = 'GRANT_CAPABILITY'
-- command.action_scope = 'PUBLIC_READ'
-- command.expires_at > now()
-- command.signature_algorithm indicates actual WebAuthn verification
-- canonical_payload.activation_scope = 'TRANSPORT_PROOF_SINGLE_REQUEST'
-- canonical_payload.transport_proof_target_url = 'https://example.com/'
-- canonical_payload.transport_proof_max_requests = 1
-- canonical_payload.authorize_owner_lockdown_release_for_transport_proof_only = true
-- canonical_payload.owner_lockdown_release_max_seconds <= 120
-- canonical_payload.general_production_network_authorized = false
-- consumed nonce + allowed owner command gateway audit must match command
-- promotion shadow verifier must pass at the appropriate phase.

-- 1) BOUNDED UNLOCK
-- SECURITY DEFINER; service_role only; exact VERIFIED v3 command.
-- Atomic transaction should:
--   a. lock singleton gateway control row FOR UPDATE
--   b. re-check stabilization exit + authority regression + command intent
--   c. ensure production_network_enabled remains false
--   d. set owner_lockdown_active=false only for proof scope, with evidence containing
--      source_command_id and unlock_expires_at <= now()+120s
--   e. audit mutation
-- Must fail closed if any prerequisite is stale or missing.

-- 2) COMMAND-BOUND PILOT GRANT
-- SECURITY DEFINER; service_role only; exact same command.
-- Insert exactly one grant into pm_agent_capability_grants_v1:
--   issuer_owner_user_id = command.owner_user_id
--   grantee_agent_key = 'PAOJAI_OPERATIONS_AI'
--   allowed_actions = ARRAY['PUBLIC_READ']
--   allowed_resources = fixed public HTTPS proof scope only
--   risk_ceiling = 'LOW'
--   can_delegate = false
--   valid_from = now()
--   expires_at <= now()+interval '10 minutes'
--   status = 'ACTIVE' only if current gateway/grant policy explicitly accepts it;
--            otherwise use the exact live accepted status determined at implementation time
--   source_command_id = command.command_id
--   evidence contains no secrets and binds the exact proof intent
-- Must duplicate-check source_command_id and refuse a second live grant.

-- 3) ATOMIC ONE-REQUEST RESERVATION
-- SECURITY DEFINER; service_role only.
-- Input: unique request_token UUID generated by trusted proof executor.
-- Required implementation pattern: one atomic conditional mutation, e.g.
--   UPDATE pm_internet_transport_proof_lane_v1
--      SET network_request_count = network_request_count + 1,
--          updated_at = now(),
--          updated_by = 'pm_internet_transport_proof_reserve_request_v1'
--    WHERE lane_key='CONTROLLED_INTERNET_TRANSPORT_PROOF'
--      AND enabled=true
--      AND proof_completed=false
--      AND network_request_count < max_requests
--   RETURNING ...;
-- A separate request-token ledger/unique constraint is required so the same token cannot
-- reserve twice. Reservation occurs BEFORE DNS or any external network side effect.
-- Failure policy is NO AUTORELEASE: once acquired, the slot remains consumed even if
-- DNS/TLS/timeout/network execution fails.

-- 4) IDEMPOTENT FINALIZE
-- SECURITY DEFINER; service_role only.
-- Input: request_token, outcome, evidence.
-- Unique request token must exist and belong to the reservation.
-- Finalize may transition a request record once; repeated identical finalize calls return
-- the existing result without changing network_request_count.
-- It MUST NOT decrement a consumed slot or reopen the lane.
-- On successful proof, set proof_completed=true and persist DNS/redirect evidence booleans
-- only from direct runtime evidence. Always audit.

-- PRIVILEGES (for all four functions)
-- REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION ... FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
-- GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION ... TO service_role;

